fe R.", "watch": "If Nixon consolidates Democratic support and closes the fundraising gap, another round of tied polls could move this toward Tossup.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Incumbent Ashley Moody (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Appointed Senator Ashley Moody enters the general election as a clear favorite over state Representative Angie Nixon, the Democratic nominee and a democratic socialist who won a competitive primary. Florida's five-point Republican lean, Moody's incumbency, and a massive financial advantage — she has raised over $11 million to Nixon's under $1 million — all work in her favor.\n\nRecent polls mostly show Moody ahead by six to eleven points, though two September surveys had the race tied, and markets still give Nixon only about a one-in-ten chance. Every major race rater puts this in the Republican column, most calling it Likely or Solid R. A Moody win is expected, but the polling variance leaves some room for doubt.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.1404, "margin": -5.31}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.2259, "margin": -4.8}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.1936, "margin": -5.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.1439, "margin": -6.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.1034, "margin": -6.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0984, "margin": -7.0}]}